# Active .claudeignore for the foundation repo itself.
# Derived from .ai-workspace/templates/claudeignore-template.md, three-header structure.
# NEVER ignore all of .ai-workspace/ — the boot files and state/ must stay readable.
# Do NOT ignore src/ or .claude/skills/ — the harness layer must stay readable so
# Claude can run, lint, and edit it.

# === 1. SECRETS (always ignore, non-negotiable) ===
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
secrets/
credentials/
**/password*
**/api-key*
**/auth-token*
.claude/settings.local.json

# === 2. PRIVACY / PII (project-specific; add via adapter) ===
# Foundation default ships no PII patterns from real projects.
# Adapters working with sensitive content add patterns here.

# === 3. TOKEN-SAVING (foundation default) ===
.ai-workspace/scratch/
.ai-workspace/archive/
.ai-workspace/research/_raw/
.ai-workspace/adapters/*/private/
# Harness build/run noise — code stays readable, only generated bulk is hidden:
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.uaw-runs/

# === 4. DO NOT ignore the rest of .ai-workspace/ or the harness ===
# The four boot files, state/, src/harness/, and .claude/skills/ must remain visible.
